WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.260
(upbeat music)
(lasers whooshing)

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.441
- [Narrator] From Pokemon Unite,

00:00:04.441 --> 00:00:06.170
(dramatic music)
(weapon whooshing)

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.600
to League of Legends, and Fortnite.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.820
- All right, listen up.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.940
- [Narrator] These are some of
the most popular video games

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.150
in the world.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.930
And behind them is a Chinese company

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.440
you may not be familiar with.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.370
- Tencent is China's largest
social media company.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.980
It is also the world's largest

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.440
video game company by revenue.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.790
- [Narrator] Last year it
reported more than $22 billion

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.840
in revenue from smartphone games

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.730
and nearly $7 billion from PC games.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.750
But that growth could hit a roadblock.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.870
Since late 2020, Beijing has embarked

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.290
on a clampdown of its
homegrown tech giants,

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.090
and Tencent is one of them.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.960
It's facing more scrutiny
over its business practices,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.657
including its allegedly
anti-competitive behaviors.

00:00:45.657 --> 00:00:47.500
Regulators are also concerned

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.810
that young Chinese citizens

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.920
may become addicted to video games.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.840
- Regulation's always looming in China.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.720
From now on, they can only
become stricter and stricter.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.210
- [Narrator] We take a look at
Tencent's vide game portfolio

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.820
over the years to see how it
became a giant in the industry

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.780
and what Beijing's regulatory crackdown

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.123
could mean for the
company's global empire.

00:01:09.999 --> 00:01:13.160
(dramatic music)

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.470
Tencent made its entrance
into the video game world

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.670
with one of the biggest
names in the industry,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.003
League of Legends.

00:01:19.003 --> 00:01:20.260
(doors beeping)

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.350
But before explaining
how Tencent got there,

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.630
you first need to understand

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.410
that it didn't start off
as a video game company.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.200
The Chinese tech giant has businesses

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.810
in music, video streaming
and search engines.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.720
But it's best known for its
social networking app WeChat,

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.790
which is everything from handling payments

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.780
to booking doctor's appointments.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.170
The app has over 1.2 billion
monthly active users,

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:43.380
and that's been key to
reaching a vast network

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.900
of gamers in China.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.510
- There's no company on the planet

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:51.126
that has this advantage that Tencent has.

00:01:51.126 --> 00:01:52.520
- [Narrator] Serkan Toto is an independent

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.780
video game industry consultant in Japan.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.470
And he's been watching this
sector for more than a decade.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.090
- They turned WeChat
into a gaming platform,

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:00.980
and they also use it

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.270
as an incredibly powerful
distribution tool,

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.630
marketing tool, user acquisition tool.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.400
They're making aggressive use of that.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.530
- [Narrator] The company has been building

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:14.060
its own online games since 2003,

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.585
developing some relatively
simple games like these.

00:02:16.585 --> 00:02:18.550
(blocks banging)

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.570
(singing in foreign language)

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.327
To more sophisticated ones.

00:02:22.327 --> 00:02:23.260
(dramatic music)
(gun shooting)

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.210
Over the years, Tencent has also tried

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.043
to export some of them.

00:02:26.043 --> 00:02:28.560
But they failed to take off in the West.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.354
- The best example is
probably Honor of Kings,

00:02:31.354 --> 00:02:32.830
(dramatic music)

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.870
which is the world's biggest
mobile game by revenue.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.770
Very well made but they are designed

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.200
to appeal to Chinese gamers, for example.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.490
The world building characters

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.493
or the stories, the narratives.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.430
- [Narrator] Video game
industry analysts say some

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.360
of Tencent's flops may have accelerated

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.426
the company's foreign investments.

00:02:52.426 --> 00:02:53.760
(dramatic music)

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.010
And this brings us back
to League of Legends.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.510
In 2009, the company became the
official Chinese distributor

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.110
of the US-developed game.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.870
- It's not a casual game, it's
not a very easy-to-play game.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:08.530
After launch, it just
developed into a crowd pleaser.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.010
- [Narrator] Toto says this kind of growth

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.100
helped push Tencent to make a bold move

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.940
with a Los Angeles startup.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.710
- [Serkan] In 2011, they made

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.990
their first big international investment

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.370
in a gaming company into Riot Games,

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:23.790
which operates one of the
world's biggest PC games,

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:25.340
League of Legends right now.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.390
- [Narrator] Tencent paid $400 million

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.290
for a 93% stake in the American company

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.380
and four years later, it
scooped up the remaining 7%,

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.900
taking full control of Riot Games.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.490
- Riot Games, they needed
funds to scale the company.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:42.140
League of Legends became big so quickly,

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.270
and on such an international scale,

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.597
mainly because of Tencent's investment.

00:03:47.597 --> 00:03:49.680
(crowd cheering)

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:50.700
- [Narrator] With Tencent's backing,

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.590
League of Legends'
monthly players have grown

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.835
by almost tenfold, and in the past decade,

00:03:54.835 --> 00:03:58.200
the game has made some
$20 billion in revenue.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.690
- This early success has
basically triggered something

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:05.510
inside Tencent, and it
showed to Tencent internally

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.160
that there's a big
opportunity, not only in China,

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.110
but also outside of China

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:12.940
if you make the right moves
in terms of investing.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.330
- [Narrator] The success
of League of Legends

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.540
helped kickstart a shopping spree.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.770
Tencent made its second big move in 2012

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:22.430
by investing in another American
game developer, Epic Games,

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:24.420
the company behind Fortnite.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.580
Activision Blizzard,
which is North America's

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.410
biggest video game
publisher by market value.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.830
Supercell, the Finnish
developer behind Clash of Clans.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.600
Bluehole, the South Korean game maker

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.450
behind the battle royale sensation PUBG.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.660
The Chinese company hasn't
just acquired stakes

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.210
but also found ways to collaborate.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.970
Roblox, the online game platform popular

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.380
with young kids entered
into a joint venture

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.010
with Tencent to make its entry into China.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.170
And the Pokemon company
worked with Tencent

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:53.970
to develop a new game
called Pokemon Unite.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.210
And as video game companies saw a big boom

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.370
during the pandemic with
people stuck at home,

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:01.300
Tencent has already closed
12 game-related deals

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.260
overseas this year.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:08.040
- Tencent has to expand
globally in the gaming market

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:12.180
because it needs to seek more growth.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.180
It also become easier for them

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.610
to get exclusive distribution rights

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.443
for these games,

00:05:17.443 --> 00:05:21.580
and that also further
cements their dominance

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:22.773
in the home market too.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.820
- [Narrator] But this dominance at home

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.480
has raised some concerns among regulators

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.660
about the gaming habits of young people.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.430
- The worst crackdown that
Tencent has faced so far

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.140
is probably the 2018 episode

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:38.110
when the Chinese government
suspended approval

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:41.370
of new games for about a year.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:42.203
- [Narrator] Then this year,

00:05:42.203 --> 00:05:44.280
as part of a larger regulatory crackdown,

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.030
Beijing became looking
more closely at Tencent.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:50.530
In August, a Chinese state
newspaper called online games

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.210
opium for the mind.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.815
Later the article was taken down,

00:05:53.815 --> 00:05:57.360
then republished without the
phrase opium for the mind.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:58.840
After the article's publication,

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.540
Tencent saw a big selloff

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.810
and its share price dropped
about 10% in just one day.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.860
- So there's a lot of confusion

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:10.860
whether that article represents
any actual policy agenda.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:13.410
- [Narrator] So Tencent has
pushed to enforce tougher rules

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.160
than required by the authorities.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.720
Young gamers will only be allowed

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.390
to play for one hour on weekdays

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.310
and two hours on weekends and holidays.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:26.310
- We haven't seen the current
regulatory storm really hit

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:28.720
the core of Tencent yet

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.310
when other companies took a very big hit.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.543
It also raises the question

00:06:34.543 --> 00:06:36.790
whether Tencent will be the next.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.920
- [Narrator] Toto says this
type of uncertainty at home

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.170
might push Tencent to see

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.810
that the bigger
opportunities are overseas.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.676
- Tencent is most likely
to even more focus

00:06:45.676 --> 00:06:48.430
on its global gaming
business going forward.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:51.670
You want to make sure that you
use your capital effectively

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:54.710
outside of China to offset certain risks.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.070
- [Narrator] Tencent said it's committed

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.070
to growing the game sector in China,

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.140
while looking at potential
investments abroad

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.070
that can bring strategic
value to the company.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:04.746
- I think that Tencent is going to try

00:07:04.746 --> 00:07:07.810
to acquire even more studios,

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:11.010
even more developers
outside its home market.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:11.843
- [Narrator] And that could mean

00:07:11.843 --> 00:07:13.550
that the next blockbuster
games you'll be playing

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.183
could have Tencent behind them.

